    "blocking": true,
    "category": "security",
    "evidence": "Probe /tmp/uri_review_R40/p1.py,p2.py with SENT='Claim your energy rebate refund at {} before the deadline.': has_link_or_contact False for '(refunds-portal i 0)', 'refunds-portal ~ i 0,', \"refunds-portal ~ 't 0'\", 'refunds-portal ~ i 0;', 'refunds-portal ~ i 0:', 'refunds-portal ~ i 0.', 'refunds-portal ~ i 0!', 'refunds-portal ~ t 0.' while '(refunds-portal i o)', '~ i o,', '~ i o.', '~ t o.' are True. For the first five: SY.verify(text[:-1]+' [1].',[src]) keeps the claim with its citation; SY.extractive returns the sentence; build_surface output contains 'refunds-portal ~ i 0,' etc. and require_valid accepts it; mask_links leaves the text unchanged. Cause: _digit_variant's fold condition `len(tok) == 1 or any(ch.isalpha() for ch in tok)` skips tokens like '0,', '0)', \"0'\", '0.'.",
    "files": [
     "uri_web/untrusted.py:906",
     "uri_web/untrusted.py:918",
     "uri_web/untrusted.py:922",
     "uri_web/untrusted.py:937",
     "uri_web/surface.py:38",
     "uri_a2ui/validate.py:150"
    ],
    "id": "R40-01",
    "owner_decision": false,
    "severity": "HIGH",
    "suggested_fix": "Decide letter/number by the token's alphanumeric core, not by the raw token: strip leading/trailing punctuation (Unicode P*/S* categories) before the length-1/has-letter test, or fold per character run of [0-9|] that is bounded by letters, spaces or punctuation unless the run is part of a number; add regression cases with trailing ',', '.', ')', ';', ':', quotes after the digit.",
    "title": "R39-01 repair incomplete (R1-01/R31-01 class): _digit_variant folds a look-alike digit only in a token with a letter or a one-character token, so a spelt ending whose last digit touches punctuation ('(refunds-portal i 0)', '~ i 0,', '~ i 0.', '~ i 0;', '~ i 0:', \"~ 't 0'\") is not a link while the letter forms are; it passes has_link_or_contact, mask_links, verify(), extractive(), the research surface and the A2UI validator (W1-AC12/AC15, D16/D29)"
   }
